auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // Auto-login: if no token is set yet, log in as the customer and stash it.
  // Guarded so it never burns the login rate-limit budget (5 / 15 min) on
  // repeat runs, and skipped for /auth/* so it doesn't double-login.
  // Credentials come from bruno/.env (process.env) — nothing secret is committed.
  const url = (req.getUrl && req.getUrl()) || "";
  const haveToken = bru.getEnvVar("token");
  if (!haveToken && url.indexOf("/api/v1/auth/") === -1) {
    const axios = require("axios");
    const base = bru.getEnvVar("baseUrl");
    const form = new URLSearchParams();
    form.append("username", bru.getProcessEnv("BRUNO_EMAIL"));
    form.append("password", bru.getProcessEnv("BRUNO_PASSWORD"));
    const res = await axios.post(base + "/api/v1/auth/login", form, {
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
    });
    bru.setEnvVar("token", res.data.access_token);
    console.log("Auto-logged in as", bru.getProcessEnv("BRUNO_EMAIL"));
  }
}

docs {
  # Ecommerce Store API

  Bruno collection scaffolded from the FastAPI OpenAPI schema.

  ## Quick start
  1. `cp bruno/.env.example bruno/.env` and fill in your local dev seed creds (`.env` is gitignored).
  2. Start the backend: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000`
  3. Select the **Local** environment (top-right), then fire any request — the collection-level
     pre-request **auto-logs-in as the customer** and injects the bearer the first time.
  4. To act as **admin**, run `01-auth > Login (admin)` once — it overwrites `token`.
  5. On a `401` (access tokens expire in ~15-30 min), run a Login request again, or run
     `01-auth > Refresh` (cookie-based, 30/hour — no login-budget cost).

  ## Notes
  - `login` is **form-encoded**; field `username` is the **email**.
  - Refresh tokens ride an HttpOnly cookie (Bruno's cookie jar handles it) — not a header.
  - `token` is a **secret var** — captured at runtime, stored locally, never written to the committed file.
  - Path/query params and JSON bodies are pre-filled with example values; edit before sending writes.
}
